== Doctor Sick 1.0.0 ==
⚠ 2 JSON patch(es) didn't apply: Doctor Sick (2)
    Patch 0 (target: game:itemtypes/resource/ingot.json) in doctorsick:patches/bad.json failed because supplied path /doesnotexist/deeper/still is invalid: The json path /doesnotexist/deeper/still was not found. No such element 'doesnotexist' at the root path
  A patch is how one mod changes another's (or the game's) blocks, items and recipes. One that doesn't fit is skipped, so that change isn't in the game: the thing it was for behaves as if the mod weren't there.
  → Usually the patching mod is made for another version of what it patches. Its author can fix the patch; an update may already have.
• 1 recipe(s) or drop(s) name things that don't exist, by the mod of the missing thing: doctorsick (1)
    doctorsick:doesnotexist
  The game skips those recipes. Usually the mod expects another mod (or another version of one) to be installed.
  Everything from start-up (/doctor startup)
